{"name":"Safari Chic","hex":"#b7aa96","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"safari","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A trip into any undeveloped area to see, photograph or to hunt wild animals in their own environment.","A caravan going on a safari."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take part in a safari."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/safari"},{"term":"chic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Elegant, stylish."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Good form; style.","A person with (a particular type of) chic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Safari","blocks":[{"text":"A safari is an overland journey to observe or hunt wild animals, especially in East Africa. The so-called \"Big Five\" game animals of Africa – lion, leopard, rhinoceros, elephant, and Cape buffalo – particularly form an important part of the safari market, both for wildlife viewing and big-game hunting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Sabi_sabi_game_drive.jpg/330px-Sabi_sabi_game_drive.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safari","wikidata":"Q849944"},{"title":"Chic","blocks":[{"text":"Chic, meaning \"stylish\" or \"smart\", is an element of fashion. It was originally a French word."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chic","wikidata":"Q583454"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg/500px-Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg/500px-Ernest_Hemingway_poses_with_water_buffalo%2C_Africa%2C_1953.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con